    "body": "DISCHARGE INSTRUCTIONS — MYRINGOTOMY WITH TUBE PLACEMENT\n\nWhat to Expect\n-mild drainage (clear, blood-tinged, or yellow) from the ear(s) is common for the first few days\n-mild discomfort or a feeling of \"popping\" is normal as anesthesia wears off\n-hearing is often noticeably improved right away\n\nEar/Water Care\n-keep ears dry for the first [7] days; after that, [earplugs recommended for swimming/bathing per surgeon preference]\n-avoid submerging the head underwater (pools, lakes, bathtub) without earplugs\n-do not put anything in the ear canal\n\nMedications\n-use prescribed ear drops as directed, typically for [5-7] days\n-resume regular medications unless instructed otherwise\n\nActivity/Diet\n-resume normal activity and diet same day\n-no restrictions on flying\n\nWhen to Call ENT\n-persistent or foul-smelling drainage beyond [1] week\n-bleeding from the ear\n-fevers\n-signs the tube has fallen out early (tubes are expected to extrude on their own over 6-18 months, but early extrusion should be evaluated)\n\nFollow-Up\n-follow up with ENT in [2-4] weeks to confirm tube position and healing\n-annual hearing checks as recommended until tubes extrude"
